    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Terminologie (arts), n° 142: Basa makondio</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Terme proposé par l'Académie des langues (années 1970).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="basabasakoendoo_135">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>basabasakoendoo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>basabasakoendea</text></form></field>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>basabasakoende</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="basabasakoendoo_135_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>corbeau</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>raven, crow</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.1 Types of animals"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>a crow-like bird, larger than the kùèndòò</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 3 occurrences, first GEN.8.7; Lexique kissi–français, p. 4: basabasakondoo; Childs 2000, p. 8: bàsàbàsà-kùèndóó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Le Lexique kissi–français écrit basabasakondoo (p. 4) et balamasakondoo (p. 3) « oiseau noir et blanc (corbeau) ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="basande_136">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>basande</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>basandio</text></form></field>
    <sense id="basande_136_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>ornement de coiffure des excisées (herbe tressée dans les cheveux)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>hair ornament of excised girls (grass braided into the hair)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.4.3 Care for hair"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.9.5 Practice religion"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Paulme 1964, p. 6: basande, pl. basandyo</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Paulme : sande « herbe ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="básí_137">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>básí</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="básí_137_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Adjective"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>jaune</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>yellow</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.3.3 Light"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 9: básí</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="basi taando_138">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>basi taando</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="basi taando_138_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>tabatière</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>snuffbox</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.2.4 Tobacco"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>tobacco, snuff</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 159: basi taando; Lexique kissi–français, p. 4: basi taando; Childs 2000, p. 347: tàáŋndó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Le second élément correspond à tàáŋndó « tabac » chez Childs.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="basia_139">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>basia</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="basia_139_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>objet magique (figuration d'arc)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>magic object (representing a bow)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.9.8 Religious things"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Paulme 1964, p. 6: basia</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="básíó_140">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>básíó</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>básíéí</text></form></field>
    <sense id="básíó_140_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>arbre à teinture jaune (bois de cam ?) ; tissu teint avec</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>tree giving a yellow dye (camwood?); cloth dyed with it</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.5.1 Tree"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.6.1 Working with cloth"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 9: básíó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="basɔɔ_141">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>basɔɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>basu</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>basunin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="basɔɔ_141_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>balayer</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>sweep</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.6.5 Sweep, rake"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>sweep, clear</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 2 occurrences, first 1KI.14.10; Keita 1979, p. 114: Basöö; Paulme 1964, p. 8: i gbasu, i basu; Lexique kissi–français, p. 4: basɔɔ/ basu, besu; Childs 2000, p. 9: bàsɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Le Lexique kissi–français donne aussi : besu. Paulme 1964, p. 8 : i gbasu, i basu « je balaie » ; le basu tyɛyo « balayez la case ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="bátákálàá_142">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>bátákálàá</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>bátákálàláŋ</text></form></field>
    <sense id="bátákálàá_142_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>peau brunie par l'exposition répétée au feu</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>skin darkened by repeated exposure to fire</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.1.4 Skin"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 9: bátákálàá</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="batayɔnndo_143">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>batayɔnndo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="batayɔnndo_143_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>bataillon</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>battalion</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.8.3 War"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Terminologie (histoire), n° 109: Batayönndo</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Terme proposé par l'Académie des langues (années 1970). Emprunt au français.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="batisio_144">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>batisio</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>batisi</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="batisio_144_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>baptiser ; baptême</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>baptize; baptism</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.9.5 Practice religion"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Lexique kissi–français, p. 4: batisio/ batisi</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Emprunt au français. La Bible dit yinɔɔ « baptiser ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="bau_145">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>bau</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="bau_145_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Connective"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>car, puisque</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>for, because</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.5 Conjunctions"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 83 occurrences, first GEN.9.6; Lexique kissi–français, p. 4: bau</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="bàú_146">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>bàú</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="bàú_146_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Ideophone"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>mouvement brusque, soudain</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>sudden movement</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.8 Ideophones"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 9: bàú</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="bàùwé_147">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>bàùwé</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="bàùwé_147_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>couteau à sculpter le bois</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>wood-carving knife</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.6.3 Working with wood"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.7.1 Cutting tool"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 9: bàùwé</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="bavo_148">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>bavo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>baolan</text></form></field>
    <sense id="bavo_148_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>gaule pour abattre les fruits</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>pole for knocking down fruit</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.2.5 Harvest"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.7 Tool"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Paulme 1964, p. 6: bawo, pl. baorã</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="bawlan_149">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>bawlan</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>bawla</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="bawlan_149_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>crochets, agrafes</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>hooks, clasps</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.7.5 Fastening tool"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 6 occurrences, first EXO.26.6</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Pluriel ; le singulier n'est pas relevé.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="bawve_150">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>bawve</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="bawve_150_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>outil pour tailler les manches de houe ou de hache</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>tool for carving hoe or axe handles</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.6.3 Working with wood"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.7.1 Cutting tool"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Lexique kissi–français, p. 4: bawve</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="bawvo_151">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>bawvo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="bawvo_151_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>fourche, support ; cheville (pour suspendre)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>forked prop, support; peg (to hang things on)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.7 Tool"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.5.2 Parts of a building"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 2 occurrences, first ISA.40.12; Lexique kissi–français, p. 4: bawvo</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Le Lexique : « la fourche qui soutient qqch. ». En EZK.15.3, bawvo est la cheville où l'on suspend des objets.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="bayiaa_152">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>bayiaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>bayiaanin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="bayiaa_152_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>attacher, fixer, coudre (sur)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>fasten, attach, sew on</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.5.2 Join, attach"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 23 occurrences, first GEN.27.16</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="bayian_153">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>bayian</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="bayian_153_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>s'attacher, se ceindre (de) ; enlacer</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>tie on oneself, gird oneself; entangle</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.5.4 Tie"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 3 occurrences, first 2SA.22.5</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Moyen de bayiaa.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="bayullo_154">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>bayullo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="bayullo_154_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>liane servant à faire les ponts de lianes (tallo)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>liana used to make vine bridges (tallo)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.5.3 Grass, herb, vine"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.5.4 Infrastructure"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Lexique kissi–français, p. 4: bayullo</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="baŋa_155">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>baŋa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="baŋa_155_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>sauver, délivrer</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>save, deliver</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.4 Prosperity, trouble"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.9.5 Practice religion"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>release, free, redeem</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 303 occurrences, first GEN.14; Childs 2000, p. 7: bàŋàá</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="baŋa_156">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>baŋa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>baŋala</text></form></field>
    <sense id="baŋa_156_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>pluriarc ; cithare sur cuvette (jouet musical)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>pluriarc; trough zither (musical toy)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.2.3 Music"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Paulme 1964, p. 5: bãŋa, pl. baŋara</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Homographe de baŋa « sauver ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="bàŋà-kpààŋndó_157">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>bàŋà-kpààŋndó</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="bàŋà-kpààŋndó_157_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>oiseau noir de la haute forêt qui mange le riz mûrissant</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>black bird of the high forest that eats ripening rice</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.1 Types of animals"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 7: bàŋà-kpààŋndó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="baŋaa_158">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>baŋaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>baŋa</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>baŋanin</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>baŋan</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="baŋaa_158_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>délivrer, sauver ; racheter</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>deliver, save, set free; redeem, buy back</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.4 Prosperity, trouble"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 199 occurrences, first GEN.19.20; Keita 1979, p. 110: Banhaa; Lexique kissi–français, p. 4: baŋaa/ baŋa; Childs 2000, p. 7: bàŋàá</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>baŋan : moyen « être sauvé, se libérer ». Lexique kissi–français, p. 4 : « racheter ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="baŋan_159">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>baŋan</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>baŋanin</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>baŋanndo</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="baŋan_159_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>être sauvé, être racheté</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>be saved, be redeemed</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.4 Prosperity, trouble"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 24 occurrences, first GEN.45.7; Childs 2000, p. 8: bàŋǎŋndó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Moyen de baŋa « sauver ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="baŋannde_160">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>baŋannde</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="baŋannde_160_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>expiation, rachat (faleŋii baŋannde)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>atonement (faleŋii baŋannde)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.9.5 Practice religion"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 39 occurrences, first EXO.30.10</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Dérivé de baŋan « être sauvé ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="bàŋánɔ̀ɔ́_161">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>bàŋánɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>bàŋáá</text></form></field>
    <sense id="bàŋánɔ̀ɔ́_161_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>oiseau du riz rouge, noir et blanc (œufs bleus)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>red, black and white rice bird (lays blue eggs)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.1 Types of animals"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 7: bàŋánɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="baŋnun_162">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>baŋnun</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="baŋnun_162_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>bâtir (pour soi) ; être bâti ; insister, presser (quelqu'un)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>build (for oneself); be built; insist, urge</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.5 Working with buildings"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 20 occurrences, first GEN.11.4</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Moyen de baŋɔɔ.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="baŋullo_163">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>baŋullo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>baŋul</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>beŋul</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="baŋullo_163_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>boucher, fermer ; rapiécer ; remplir (un trou, un puits)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>stop up, close; patch; fill in (a hole, a well)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.3.6 Open"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>fill in or close a hole</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 3 occurrences, first 1KI.11.27; Keita 1979, p. 114: Banhullo; Lexique kissi–français, p. 4: baŋullo/ baŋul, beŋul; Childs 2000, p. 8: bàŋùlló</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>beŋul : radical négatif (MRK 2,21). Lexique kissi–français, p. 4-5 : « rapiécer ; remplir un trou, un puits ; boucher les oreilles » (aussi beŋullo/ beŋul).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="bàŋúlló_164">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>bàŋúlló</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="bàŋúlló_164_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>bouchon fermant l'entrée d'un terrier</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>plug closing the entrance of an animal's burrow</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.5 Animal home"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 8: bàŋúlló</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="baŋulu_165">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>baŋulu</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="baŋulu_165_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>boucher (une ouverture, les oreilles)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>stop up, plug (an opening, one's ears)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.3.6 Open"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 1 occurrences, first ZEC.7.11; Paulme 1964, p. 5: baŋulu</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Paulme : i baŋulu mɛnde « j'ai bouché l'eau (calebasse renversée sur une autre) » ; i baŋulu hɛnkɛyo a kamadole « j'ai bouché le bol avec de la cire ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="baŋulufaa_166">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>baŋulufaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="baŋulufaa_166_s1">
