    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 110: fɔ́yɔ́ŋndó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="fɔ́ŋɔ́fɔ́ŋɔ́ɔ́_1504">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>fɔ́ŋɔ́fɔ́ŋɔ́ɔ́</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>fɔ́ŋɔ́fɔ́ŋúá</text></form></field>
    <sense id="fɔ́ŋɔ́fɔ́ŋɔ́ɔ́_1504_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>calao</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>hornbill</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.1 Types of animals"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 109: fɔ́ŋɔ́fɔ́ŋɔ́ɔ́</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="fɔɔ_1505">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>fɔɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="check"/>
    <sense id="fɔɔ_1505_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Particle"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>quant à ; jusqu'à ; pour autant que (?)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>as for; until; as far as (?)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.6 Particles"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Lexique kissi–français, p. 16: fɔɔ; Sandara Kisia, fable 3: fɔɔ</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Les points d'interrogation sont dans la source. Sandara Kissia, fable 3 : mo tosa lende, fɔɔ palɛi ndi ya « il fit ainsi, jusqu'au jour … » (sens « jusqu'à » probable).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="fɔ́ɔ́_1506">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>fɔ́ɔ́</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>fɔ̂láŋ</text></form></field>
    <sense id="fɔ́ɔ́_1506_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>pulpe de la noix de palme</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>palm-nut pulp</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.2.3 Types of food"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.5.5 Parts of a plant"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 109: fɔ́ɔ́</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="fɔ́ɔ́fɔ̀_1507">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>fɔ́ɔ́fɔ̀</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="fɔ́ɔ́fɔ̀_1507_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Adverb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>aussitôt, soudain</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>immediately, suddenly</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.2 Adverbs"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.4.8 Speed"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>spot, place; on the spot, right away</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 139 occurrences, first JOS.6.20; Paulme 1964, p. 27: fɔfɔ; Childs 2000, p. 108: fòòfóó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Paulme 1964, p. 27 : fɔfɔ « aussitôt » (i tosani fɔfɔ « je le ferai aussitôt »).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="fɔ̀ɔ̀làá_1508">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>fɔ̀ɔ̀làá</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="fɔ̀ɔ̀làá_1508_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>souffrir ; sécher à moitié</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>suffer; partly dry, dry up</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.4.2 Feel bad"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.3.3 Wet"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 109: fɔ̀ɔ̀làá</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="fɔ̀ɔ̀mɔ̀lɛ́ŋ_1509">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>fɔ̀ɔ̀mɔ̀lɛ́ŋ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="le"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>fɔ̀ɔ̀mùɛ́í</text></form></field>
    <sense id="fɔ̀ɔ̀mɔ̀lɛ́ŋ_1509_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>plante à feuilles comestibles</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>plant with edible leaves</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.5.3 Grass, herb, vine"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.2.3 Types of food"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 109: fɔ̀ɔ̀mɔ̀lɛ́ŋ</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="fɔɔndu_1510">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>fɔɔndu</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="fɔɔndu_1510_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>plante médicinale (contre le ma ; purification par aspersion)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>medicinal plant (against the ma; purification by sprinkling)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.5 Plant"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.5.7 Treat disease"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.9.5 Practice religion"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Paulme 1964, p. 27: fɔɔndu</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Paulme : l'écorce donne un remède contre le ma ; le sarino asperge avec ses feuilles.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="fɛ́-fɛ́i_1511">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>fɛ́-fɛ́i</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="fɛ́-fɛ́i_1511_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Ideophone"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>doucement (vent) ; (hoeyii fɛ́-fɛ́i) la brise légère</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>gently (wind); (hoeyii fɛ́-fɛ́i) the light breeze</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.8 Ideophones"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.1.3 Weather"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>sound of wind blowing gently</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 1 occurrences, first GEN.3.8; Childs 2000, p. 103: fé-fé</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Une seule occurrence : o hoeyii fɛ́-fɛ́i paale delɛi nin « à la brise du soir » (GEN.3.8).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="fɛ̀fɔ̀ɔ́_1512">
