    <sense id="kíŋ-kìŋ_2152_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Ideophone"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>pas lourds (soldat, éléphant)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>heavy footsteps (soldier, elephant)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.8 Ideophones"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.2.1 Manner of movement"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 168: kíŋ-kìŋ</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kíŋgìó_2153">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kíŋgìó</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>kíŋgìá</text></form></field>
    <sense id="kíŋgìó_2153_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>rat des palmiers à queue d'écureuil ; gros porc mâle</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>palm rat with a squirrel-like tail; large male pig</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.1 Types of animals"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 168: kíŋgìó kíŋgìá</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kiŋikiŋio_2154">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kiŋikiŋio</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>kiŋikiŋi</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="kiŋikiŋio_2154_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>découper</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>cut up</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.8.3 Cut"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 110: Kinhikinhio; Lexique kissi–français, p. 24: kiŋikiŋio/ kiŋikiŋi; Terminologie (arts), n° 143: Kinhikinhioo, Piimiaa</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Redoublement. Académie des langues (terminologie, arts n° 143 et 144) : kinhikinhioo (aussi piimiaa) « hachurer, hachure ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kìŋndáŋ_2155">
